From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Aug 2021 10:11:12 +0200
Subject: Fix openssl memory leaks

Some leaks that snuck in during refactorings.

Only the openssl_csr_get_public_key() part is needed here: the key
returned by X509_REQ_get_pubkey() has to be freed after "Extract public
key portion via PEM roundtrip". The other part is for code that PHP 7.2
does not have.

(cherry picked from commit 7d2a2c7dc0447c81316d14f3a43a4b6a8ce0b982)
---
 ext/openssl/openssl.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/openssl/openssl.c b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
index 1c0db26..1463c26 100644
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -3660,7 +3660,7 @@ PHP_FUNCTION(openssl_csr_get_public_key)
 	zend_resource *csr_resource;
 
 	X509_REQ *csr;
-	EVP_PKEY *tpubkey;
+	EVP_PKEY *orig_key, *tpubkey;
 
 	if (zend_parse_parameters(ZEND_NUM_ARGS(), "z|b", &zcsr, &use_shortnames) == FAILURE) {
 		return;
@@ -3673,7 +3673,9 @@ PHP_FUNCTION(openssl_csr_get_public_key)
 	}
 
 	/* Retrieve the public key from the CSR */
-	tpubkey = php_openssl_extract_public_key(X509_REQ_get_pubkey(csr));
+	orig_key = X509_REQ_get_pubkey(csr);
+	tpubkey = php_openssl_extract_public_key(orig_key);
+	EVP_PKEY_free(orig_key);
 
 	if (!csr_resource) {
 		/* We need to free the original CSR if it was freshly created */
